  <h2 style="font-size: 14pt; margin-top: 20px;">General Instructions</h2>
  <p style="font-size: 10pt;">Note: Form 1040-T references are to a new form sent to certain individuals on a test basis.</p>

  <h2 style="font-size: 14pt; margin-top: 20px;">A Change To Note</h2>
  <p style="font-size: 10pt;">We have combined Form 4868-V (payment voucher) and Form 4868 into one, smaller, detachable Form 4868. The form is at the bottom of this page.</p>

  <h2 style="font-size: 14pt; margin-top: 20px;">Purpose of Form</h2>
  <p style="font-size: 10pt;">Use Form 4868 to apply for 4 more months to file Form 1040EZ, Form 1040A, Form 1040, or Form 1040-T.</p>
  <p style="font-size: 10pt;">To get the extra time you MUST:</p>
  <ul style="font-size: 10pt; margin-top: 5px;">
    <li>Properly estimate your 1995 tax liability using the form available to you.</li>
    <li>Enter your tax liability on line 6a of Form 4868.</li>
    <li>Sign your Form 4868.</li>
    <li>File Form 4868 by the regular due date of your return.</li>
  </ul>
  <p style="font-size: 10pt;">If you cannot pay the entire balance due, see the instructions for line 6c.</p>
  <p style="font-size: 10pt;">You do not have to explain why you are asking for the extension. We will contact you only if your request is denied.</p>
  <p style="font-size: 10pt;">Do not file Form 4868 if you want the IRS to figure your tax or you are under a court order to file your return by the regular due date.</p>
  <p style="font-size: 10pt;">For Paperwork Reduction Act Notice, see page 3.</p>
</div>

